  "notes": "{落胆|らくたん} expresses disappointment or discouragement, typically at a deeper level than casual disappointment.\n\nFORMS:\n{落|らく} (fall) + {胆|たん} (courage/spirit) — literally \"one's spirit falls\"\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- 〜⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{落胆|らくたん}する: to be disappointed by ~\n- {落胆|らくたん}⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{隠|かく}せない→隠す：02034_kakusu⟧: unable to hide disappointment\n- {落胆|らくたん}している⟦{場合|ばあい}→場合：01704_baai⟧⟦では→では：02945_deha⟧⟦ない→ない：01118_nai⟧: no time to be dejected\n\nREGISTER:\nMore formal and literary than がっかり. Common in news reports, written language, and formal speech.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦がっかり→がっかり：00054_gakkari⟧: disappointed (casual, everyday)\n- ⟦{失望|しつぼう}→失望：03183_shitsubou⟧: disappointment (also formal)",
